  ],
  "equipment_type": "Self-contained unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Carrier 50BV and 50VQP indoor water-cooled self-contained units and 50BVW units with the factory SCU Open program on a UC Open XP controller.",
  "summary": "The SCU Open program runs on a UC Open XP controller and talks BACnet MS/TP or ARC156 on its EIA-485 port. The points list has 168 objects: setpoints and configuration as AVs, alarms and enables as BVs, and a few multistate values such as BAS On/Off and System Mode. It covers single-zone (space temperature) and VAV (supply air temperature and duct static) operation, plus water economizer, hot gas reheat and auxiliary hot water heat options.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object IDs are printed as AV:3001 style references; access is from the Point Access column (R/W listed as writable).",
    "The four occupied/unoccupied heating and cooling setpoints (AV 3001-3004) are printed only as \"Setpoint\" in the name column; their descriptions here come from the BACnet point names.",
    "Water economizer, hot gas reheat, auxiliary heat, humidity and CO2 points only apply when those options are installed and enabled.",
    "ARC156 is a Carrier-specific 156 kbps network; third-party systems connect over BACnet MS/TP."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "50BVT, 50BVV, 50BVQ 024-034, 50VQP 210-360 (Cooling Only), and 50BVW with SCU Open Controller - Controls, Start-Up, Operation and Troubleshooting (Appendix B, BACnet Points List)",
